{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "birch-1",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "root-preparation-surface",
      "reason": "The implemented extension already assesses an actual fractional bark sheet and hard contact, then enables paid preparation of at most one root on a physically sufficient surface. It does not require a whole bark unit. Your listed bark and stones are candidates, not proof of suitability: connected sheet geometry, accessible firm support and tool contact must pass the actual assessment. Individual mastery of root-preparation is required before learning this extension; neither implementation nor this review grants mastery.",
      "specification": "Reuse root-preparation-surface unchanged, with root-preparation as its existing learning prerequisite. Its learning duration is 1 round, separate from the prerequisite's 2 rounds. Consult its full current contract for exact references and execution parameters. assess-surface takes barkId, toolId and optional site{x,y}, costing one round and 0.2 energy. Validate actual ownership, availability, reachable shared geometry, firm support and a connected bark rectangle at least 0.16 by 0.16 m; use represented geometry first and only the registered uncertain mass-conserving fallback where permitted. Do not treat bark fines as a connected sheet. prepare-small uses the assessed setup and an actual eligible root portion, capped at one root, with the registered proportional paid work. Retain reusable implements, food composition, toxicity, age and provenance; crushing supplies no cooking, healing or preservation effect. Use the existing progress, remaining-work and cancellation contract, including death cancellation and conservation of escrowed tools and partial food at the actual worksite. No new schema, materials, recipe, migration or duplicate feedback source is needed.",
      "experienceReview": "Use the existing information-confirmed rule only if an actual assessment or experiment establishes personally new, qualified information: performer receives 0.8, source cap 1, held 8 rounds, refresh subject to cooldown 12; maintained gain 0.035 with decay 0.0015 under the registered rule. Re-reading an already established result does not qualify. Completed paid preparation may trigger the existing practice-confirmed rule only at its registered qualified milestones: 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8, refresh with cooldown 12, maintained gain 0.02 and decay 0.001. Do not create alias rewards or award mastery, requesting or learning. No separate pleasure or physical-comfort benefit follows from assessment or crushing alone; any later eating uses actual consumption and existing meal rules.",
      "visualReview": "Bind the existing root-surface-assessed event to a dated suitability result showing measured or explicitly modeled sheet dimensions, contact/support checks and any failure reason. Show actual preparation progress and changed food through food-preparation-started and food-preparation-completed; show cancellation through root-preparation-stopped. Replay must retain the referenced physical setup, paid work and actual partial or completed output, without displaying a whole bark unit, new stock or a successful preparation before execution.",
      "learning": 1
    }
  ]
}

